/*
==============================================================================
  PoC 01b -- CONTROL for PoC 01.  Not a defect: this file behaves CORRECTLY.
==============================================================================

  This is the same protocol and the same lemma as
  attacks/01_last_induction_unsound.spthy, with the restriction expressed
  using a guarded existential instead of `last()`.

  Both restrictions are non-prefix-closed:

      01  : "All x #i. Start(x) @ i ==> not(last(#i))"
            [Start(x)] violates it, [Start(x),Step(x)] satisfies it.

      01b : "All x #i. Start(x) @ i ==> Ex #j. Step(x) @ j"
            [Start(x)] violates it, [Start(x),Step(x)] satisfies it.

  The only difference is which side of

      partition isSafetyFormula restrictions
      -- lib/theory/src/Theory/Constraint/System.hs:849

  they land on.  The existential phrasing is correctly classified as
  non-safety and conjoined into the proof obligation; the `last` phrasing is
  misclassified as safety and routed into sLemmas instead.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  TAMARIN SAYS (this file -- all correct)
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    NoStart_with_induction    (all-traces): falsified - found trace (6 steps)
    NoStart_without_induction (all-traces): falsified - found trace (4 steps)
    StartReachable            (exists-trace): verified (4 steps)

  and the restriction is NOT annotated "// safety formula".

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  TAMARIN SAYS (PoC 01, identical protocol and lemma)
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    // safety formula                                          <-- misclassified
    NoStart_with_induction    (all-traces): verified (3 steps)  <-- WRONG
    NoStart_without_induction (all-traces): falsified - found trace (2 steps)
    StartReachable            (exists-trace): verified (2 steps)

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  WHY THIS MATTERS
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  This pair rules out every alternative explanation for PoC 01's wrong
  verdict: it is not the protocol, not the lemma, not induction in general,
  and not non-prefix-closed restrictions in general -- Tamarin handles those
  correctly, as this file shows.  It is specifically the classification of
  `last` atoms by isSafetyFormula.

  Note: the most literally equivalent phrasing of `not(last(#i))` would be
  "Ex #j. #i < #j", but Tamarin rejects that as an unguarded existential
  ("unguarded variable(s) '#j'"), so the control uses a Step action as the
  guard.  This changes the restriction's exact content but not the property
  that matters here: non-prefix-closedness.

  This file is a control and is NOT exercised by run.sh (which only checks
  that defects still reproduce).  Run it directly:

      tamarin-prover --prove 01b_control_existential_phrasing.spthy
==============================================================================
*/

theory ControlGuardedExistential begin

rule Start: [ Fr(x) ] --[ Start(x) ]-> [ A(x) ]
rule Step:  [ A(x)  ] --[ Step(x)  ]-> [      ]

// Non-prefix-closed, but with a guarded existential => classified non-safety.
restriction StartImpliesStep:
  "All x #i. Start(x) @ i ==> Ex #j. Step(x) @ j"

lemma NoStart_with_induction [use_induction]:
  "All x #i. Start(x) @ i ==> F"

lemma NoStart_without_induction:
  "All x #i. Start(x) @ i ==> F"

lemma StartReachable: exists-trace
  "Ex x #i. Start(x) @ i"

end
